50 0 obj
<</A 1233 0 R /Alt
  (A diagram showing the five vocabulary generation algorithm steps. The input photograph depicting a birthday party is used as input, with a man in front of a birthday cake with lit candles. In the first step \(Scene Understanding\), the photo description "\a man sitting at a table with a birthday cake with lit candles" is created. In the second step \(Photo Description Matching\), this description is used for finding photos from VIST depicting the same situation. Three photos matching the input description \are shown as example. The three photos show a person in front of a birthday cake. In the third step, all stories associated with the selected photos are associated, as for example "everyone sang happy birthday to him", "he couldn't wait to blow his candle\s", and "I had a lovely cake on my birthday". In the fourth step, the selected phrases are processed to find clusters and their exemplars, e.g., "chocolate birthday cake with lots of candles", and also frequent words, e.g., "cake", "candle", "family", "bi\rthday", "wish", "happy". In the fifth step, the frequent words are expanded with words from a mental lexicon model, e.g., "cake" is expanded with "chocolate", "sweet", "eat", while "candle" is expanded with "light", "wax", "flame". System uncontrollable \parameters related to the input photo are stated : level of contextual information in the input photo and contextual description quality. System controllable parameters similarity threshold, selection method, and expansion size are also shown.)
  /ID (AD000000-0000-0000-ADBE-       14398) /K [1211 0 R 72] /P 8 0 R
  /Pg 410 0 R /S /Figure>>
endobj
